            <ArticleTitle>Obesity and deep brain stimulation: an overview.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>181-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5214/ans.0972.7531.220310</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Deep brain stimulation (DBS) has been employed to treat a variety of disorders such as Parkinson disease, dystonia, and essential tremor. Newer indications such as epilepsy and obsessive-compulsive disorder have been added to the armamentarium. In this review, we present an initial summary of current methods in the management of obesity and then explore efforts in neuromodulation and DBS as a novel modality in the treatment of obesity disorders.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
